'pragmat'title="module initialization".
$ A module can have its own 'root': the initialization of the module.
$ All of them run before the root of the main program. Their order is
$ not specified, except that 'wait for' runs the initialization of the
$ named module first, if it has not run yet; see manifest.ale.
$ The manifest constants _file_, _line_, _title_, _module_ and _rule_
$ are replaced by the compiler with the source file name, the line
$ number, the title, the module name and the name of the rule in
$ which they appear.
$ Shows: module roots, wait for, manifest constants.
'pragmat'require=("outlib","manifest").

'a'where am i:
   c str+"main program, rule '",c str+_rule_,c str+"' in ",
   c str+_file_,c str+", line ",c int+_line_,c char+newline.

'root'
   c str+"The main program starts: ",c str+_title_,c char+newline,
   where am i,show manifest.
'end'
